## Executive Summary

This analysis prioritizes two high-volume work streams at Apex Distribution for agentic transformation: **Delivery Exceptions** (~180/day, 12 min avg) and **Dispatch Adjustments** (~90/day, 18 min avg).

### Key Findings

**Delivery Exceptions** emerges as the **Wave 1 priority** due to:
- Higher volume (180 vs. 90 cases/day)
- Better system access (CRM API, driver app read-only)
- Lower technical complexity (no dispatch console API dependency)
- Faster payback (5-8 months vs. 18-24 months)
- Lower risk profile (reversible decisions, moderate compliance)

**Dispatch Adjustments** is sequenced to **Wave 2** due to:
- Critical API constraint (dispatch console write access)
- Higher decision complexity (driver welfare, safety, SLA risk)
- Dependency on Wave 1 learnings (HITL protocols, governance)
- Requires upfront infrastructure investment (£50-80K API wrapper)

### Economic Summary

| Work Stream | Volume | Agentic Value Score | Annual Saving | Build Cost | Payback | Wave |
|-------------|--------|---------------------|---------------|------------|---------|------|
| **Delivery Exceptions** | 180/day | **20** | £52-70K | £50-80K | 8-12 months | **1** |
| **Dispatch Adjustments** | 90/day | **16** | £35-52K | £80-120K | 18-24 months | **2** |

**Total Program Value**: £87-122K annual savings, £130-200K total investment, 15-18 month payback (phased).

### Strategic Recommendation

**Phase 1 (Months 1-6)**: Deploy Delivery Exceptions agent-led solution. Build foundational CRM integration, driver app messaging, and HITL governance. Target 40-60% cognitive work elimination.

**Phase 2 (Months 7-12)**: Deploy Dispatch Adjustments human-led + agent support. Build dispatch console API wrapper (or route optimization service) leveraging Phase 1 platform assets. Target 35-50% cognitive work elimination.

**Phase 3 (Months 13-18)**: Billing integration (optional, contingent on Phase 1-2 success metrics and business case validation).

